    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42-a2">

                <pb facs="0082" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg82"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">House of
                            Commons</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Tuesday</hi>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1861-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 9</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">notices of motions</hi>.</head>
                <p>Lord <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanley</hi>.—To ask the under secretary of
                    state for war what steps have been or are being taken to abolish purchase in the
                    army above the rank of major, as recommended by the commission of 1856.</p>
                <p>Lord <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alfred Churchill</hi>.—To ask the secretary of
                    state for foreign affairs whether it is the intention of her Majesty’s
                    government to recognize the Confederate States of America without a guarantee
                    that the flag of that confederation shall not be made subservient to the slave
                    trade, and whether it is the intention of her Majesty’s government to invite a
                    conference of the European powers on the subject, so as to prevent the African
                    slave trade being reopened or carried on under the flag of the said
                    confederation.</p>
            </div>
